WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:17.505
slid up his tunnel and went out to make arrangements for Wendy, John, and Michael's trip home.

2
00:00:18.305 --> 00:00:21.848
He gave orders to the Indians to guide Wendy and her brothers through the woods.

3
00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:27.853
Then Peter returned to the underground home, where an unfortunate sight greeted him.

4
00:00:28.954 --> 00:00:32.541
Upset that they were going to lose Wendy, the Lost Boys were frantic.

5
00:00:32.561 --> 00:00:36.805
"After you leave, things will be worse than before you came!"

6
00:00:36.825 --> 00:00:40.488
"We won't let you go."

7
00:00:40.508 --> 00:00:43.090
"We'll keep you as our prisoner."

8
00:00:43.110 --> 00:00:45.132
"Chain her up!"

9
00:00:45.572 --> 00:00:46.673
They shouted at her.

10
00:00:47.534 --> 00:00:49.155
Only Tootles protected Wendy.

11
00:00:50.056 --> 00:00:52.258
He took out his sword and faced the other boys.

12
00:00:53.359 --> 00:00:55.180
This wasn't like the usual Tootles.

13
00:00:56.661 --> 00:00:59.424
He stood up tall and straight and proud.

14
00:01:00.844 --> 00:01:06.748
"I will strike the first one who does not behave well toward Wendy," he said bravely.

15
00:01:07.689 --> 00:01:09.070
The other boys backed off.

16
00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:11.411
Then they noticed Peter.

17
00:01:12.412 --> 00:01:14.413
They saw that he would not support them either.

18
00:01:14.433 --> 00:01:21.318
"I would never," said Peter, "keep a girl in Neverland against her will.

19
00:01:22.459 --> 00:01:26.802
I've asked the Indians to guide you through the woods," he explained to Wendy.

20
00:01:26.822 --> 00:01:30.144
"Then Tinker Bell will take you across the sea.

21
00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:32.289
Wake Tinker Bell up, Nibs."

22
00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:37.332
Nibs knocked twice on the wall beside Tinker Bell's nook.

23
00:01:38.413 --> 00:01:42.276
Her curtains were drawn, but of course she had been listening all along.

24
00:01:43.416 --> 00:01:48.440
The fairy was delighted that Wendy was leaving, but she did not want to be her guide.

25
00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:52.182
Without opening her curtains, she refused.

26
00:01:52.202 --> 00:01:55.705
"Tink says she won't go!"

27
00:01:56.425 --> 00:01:57.145
Nibs yelled.

28
00:01:58.146 --> 00:02:00.648
He was surprised that she dared to disobey Peter.

29
00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:04.102
Peter went directly to Tinker Bell himself.

30
00:02:04.122 --> 00:02:10.747
"Tink," he demanded, "if you don't get up and dress at once, I will open your curtains.

31
00:02:11.647 --> 00:02:13.669
Then we will see you in your nightgown."

32
00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:17.772
This made the vain fairy leap to the floor.

33
00:02:17.792 --> 00:02:20.654
"Who said I wasn't getting up?"

34
00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:21.754
she cried.

35
00:02:22.715 --> 00:02:27.178
Meanwhile, Wendy, John, and Michael were getting ready for their journey.

36
00:02:28.259 --> 00:02:32.950
The Lost Boys watched, growing sadder and sadder at the thought of Wendy leaving.

37
00:02:34.291 --> 00:02:41.316
When they began to cry, Wendy softly said, "Dear boys, if you want to come with me, I'm

38
00:02:41.416 --> 00:02:43.918
sure my mother and father will adopt you."

39
00:02:45.199 --> 00:02:50.222
This invitation was actually meant for Peter, but she offered it to the rest of the boys out

40
00:02:50.242 --> 00:02:50.823
of kindness.

41
00:02:50.843 --> 00:02:54.986
"Peter, can we go with Wendy?"

42
00:02:55.606 --> 00:02:56.107
they asked.

43
00:02:56.127 --> 00:02:59.865
"All right," he said with a bitter smile.

44
00:03:00.846 --> 00:03:02.788
They went to pack their knapsacks for the trip.

45
00:03:03.788 --> 00:03:07.071
Wendy and the boys both thought Peter would be joining them.

46
00:03:08.112 --> 00:03:11.334
But Peter, of course, had no intention of going.

47
00:03:11.355 --> 00:03:15.178
"Get your things, Peter," said Wendy.

48
00:03:15.198 --> 00:03:19.281
"No," he answered, pretending not to care.

49
00:03:19.301 --> 00:03:21.363
"I'm not going with you."

50
00:03:22.243 --> 00:03:27.868
Then to show that none of this mattered to him, he skipped around the room playing his flute.

51
00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:31.709
"Don't you want to find your mother?"

52
00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:33.090
Wendy asked.

53
00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:35.551
She didn't want to leave him behind.

54
00:03:35.571 --> 00:03:40.614
"Even if I had one, I hardly remember her," said Peter.

55
00:03:40.634 --> 00:03:44.096
"Anyway, she would just force me to grow up.

56
00:03:44.616 --> 00:03:47.238
And I want to stay a little boy and have fun."

57
00:03:48.759 --> 00:03:54.362
When Wendy told the boys that Peter wasn't coming, they wondered if he would let them go without

58
00:03:54.422 --> 00:04:00.157
him. "Let's not make a fuss," said Peter, too proud to show his feelings.

59
00:04:00.177 --> 00:04:02.117
"Good-bye, boys.

60
00:04:02.357 --> 00:04:03.317
Good-bye, Wendy."

61
00:04:03.958 --> 00:04:05.198
He held out his hand to her.

62
00:04:06.138 --> 00:04:09.759
She took it sadly, but wished he had hugged or kissed her instead.

63
00:04:09.779 --> 00:04:16.281
"Please remember to eat properly, Peter," she said, almost crying.

64
00:04:16.301 --> 00:04:19.062
"And don't forget to take your medicine.

65
00:04:19.642 --> 00:04:21.262
I've put it in a cup for you."

66
00:04:22.483 --> 00:04:23.723
A sad moment followed.

67
00:04:24.543 --> 00:04:28.246
The sadness made Peter uncomfortable, so he interrupted the silence.

68
00:04:28.266 --> 00:04:30.187
"Are you ready, Tink?"

69
00:04:30.808 --> 00:04:31.489
he called out.

70
00:04:31.509 --> 00:04:33.130
"Lead the way."

71
00:04:34.692 --> 00:04:37.655
Tinker Bell darted up the nearest tunnel to the outside world.

72
00:04:38.535 --> 00:04:43.761
But before anyone could follow her, the sound of a brutal battle erupted above.

73
00:04:44.842 --> 00:04:49.946
At that very moment, the pirates had attacked the Indians on top of the Lost Boys' home.
